 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical Application Circuit",
   "page": 8,
   "description": "A complete microphone conditioner on one supply. The microphone signal comes in through a 0.1 µF capacitor, since INPUT sits near 400 mV. A 10 µF capacitor carries the buffered signal from BUFOUT to VCAIN. AVG CAP has a 10 µF electrolytic to ground for the rms detector. RGATE and RCOMP from pins 7 and 8 to VDD set the noise gate threshold and the compression ratio from the two setting tables. A 500 kΩ pull-up keeps SHUTDOWN high unless the control line pulls it low. The output, near 1.4 V dc, leaves through a 10 µF electrolytic with a 100 kΩ load to ground; VDD has a 10 µF electrolytic to ground.",
